# Blueprint CMS – building history

## 2026-10-25 – First task: routing content

- Dependencies: notrab/dumbo (HTTP/PSR-7, router), illuminate/support (Collection, Arr), michelf/php-markdown,
  symfony/yaml (front matter – not in the spec, but needed to parse yaml), pestphp/pest (dev).
- Fixed public/index.php: PROJECT_DIR is now dirname(__DIR__), autoload path pointed outside the project.
- Config: Config::load($dir) reads config.php + config.{hostname}.php (hostname sanitized, port stripped).
  App::create() adds site/config as fallback, so the project config/ (deployment) overrides site/config (project code).
- Routing: Dumbo only gets one catch-all route; content resolution happens in Site::find(). Dumbo's trailing-slash
  removal is disabled, because the canonical url depends on the content: pages with published subpages end with "/"
  (/blog -> /blog/), all others don't (/imprint/ -> /imprint). /home redirects to /. Query strings are kept.
- Pages: folder page (page.json, page.md, page.content.md, page.php) or file page ({slug}.md / {slug}.php).
  File pages are only .md/.php, which keeps site.json, users.json and redirects.json from becoming pages.
  "NN_" prefix = sort number (listed page), "." prefix = draft. Folder pages win over file pages with the same slug.
- page.php semantics (spec only showed an example that echoes + exits): it is the page's own renderer, executed at
  render time only (never while scanning, because it may have side effects). Returning an array instead merges the
  array into the page data and renders the normal template.
- Data: nested maps -> Data objects (page()->data()->some->nested), lists -> arrays, missing keys -> null, so templates
  don't fail on optional fields. Values are raw; escaping is the template's job (esc()).
- Drafts are only resolved when User::current() is set. Sessions are only started if the client sends a session
  cookie, so anonymous visitors don't get sessions. Panel login doesn't exist yet.
- redirect() throws a Redirect exception, so it works from any depth of template/partial code.
- Spec mentions both site/templates/snippets/ (folder structure) and partials (helper) – went with
  site/templates/partials/ as the helper describes.
- Errors: debug=true shows class/message/file/trace, otherwise a plain 500 page; 404 uses site/templates/404.php.
- Tests: Pest against the real content/ (routing spec) plus tests/fixtures/project for page.php,
  redirect(), config merging and slug collisions (the real content/01_blog/page.php calls exit()).

2026-10-25 – Blueprints
- Followed Kirby v6/develop (src/Blueprint/Normalizer.php): root `fields` are definitions as soon as there is a
  layout (tabs/columns/sections); tabs and columns reference them by name. Every blueprint is normalized into
  tabs -> columns -> fields (loose fields -> one 1/1 column, loose columns -> `main` tab). Legacy sections are
  converted to fields (pages -> pagelist, files -> filelist, fields section -> its fields), groups are spliced.
  Unreferenced definitions are ignored, like in Kirby.
- Split: Blueprint (loading, lookup, accessors, validation), BlueprintNormalizer (pure array transformation,
  gets a `find` closure for `extends`), Field (one field definition). The user asked for Blueprint\Field as the
  name of the definition class, so the planned per-model value object ($page->createdAt()) needs another
  name (e.g. FieldValue).
- Invalid fields (unknown type, missing reference, duplicate name, missing extends) become red `info` fields
  instead of exceptions, so one typo doesn't break the panel view (Kirby behaviour).
- Deviations from Kirby: `title: text` (string that is a field type) sets the type instead of extending; a list
  of references can contain inline definitions (`- text: {type: textarea}`); `title: true` with an existing
  root definition uses that definition. Labels: "seoTitle" -> "Seo title".
- Lookup: site/blueprints/{name}.{yml,yaml,php}, then core blueprints in src/blueprints/ (pages/default, site,
  users/default, files/default). Page blueprint: pages/{template} -> page blueprint with `default: true`
  (from the user's example page.yml) -> pages/default. User blueprint: users/{role} -> users/default.
- Raw blueprint files are cached by absolute path (static), so tests with different projects don't collide.
- Validation (required, min/max, minlength/maxlength, pattern, email/url/date/time, static options, nested
  structure/object rows) is part of the blueprint, since blueprints are the data structure definition.
- options/status normalization per model type, no i18n yet.
- Planned (user note): every blueprint field becomes a model method returning a formatted, escaped value object
  ($page->createdAt(), ->isEmpty(), ->format()); raw values stay in $page->data(). Conflicts with existing Page
  methods (title(), url(), template(), …) need to be resolved then.
- Docs in docs/ (guides, reference, examples), structured as a content folder (NN_folder/page.md with a title in
  the front matter), so the CMS can render them with contentFolder=docs. Links point to page.md files (GitHub).

2026-10-25 – User blueprint fallback, field methods
- User role defaults to "user"; blueprint lookup users/{role} -> users/user -> users/default (core).
- Field methods: HasFields trait (Page, Site, User, Values) with __call -> FieldValue. Model methods win over field
  names (PHP only calls __call for undefined methods), field("url") is the escape hatch. Page::title() now returns a
  FieldValue (falls back to the slug) – breaking, but consistent.
- FieldValue echo = formatted by type + escaped. Exceptions: textarea renders markdown with no_markup (inline html
  escaped, md() stays the raw variant), writer/list output their html as is (trusted editor content).
  password/structure/object/blocks/layout output nothing.
- Unknown methods are passed to illuminate/support: Carbon (date/time), Collection (lists), Stringable (rest).
  String results are wrapped in a FieldValue again so chaining never leaks unescaped output; empty values return an
  empty FieldValue so ->format() etc. don't fail. esc(FieldValue) returns it unchanged (no double escaping).
- List entries get a single-value type (tags -> select etc.), structure rows and objects become Values.
- Normalized blueprints are cached per file (static), since each page asks its blueprint for field definitions.

2026-10-25 – Panel
- User requirements: Kirby-like minimal UI (left sidebar + main view), Vue components, form fields as simple and
  native as possible, behind a login at /panel, communication via REST API, page rendering independent of the panel.
- Backend: Panel class with its own small regex route table (page ids contain slashes, so ids use "+" like Kirby:
  /panel/api/pages/blog+newest_entry). App's catch-all route now accepts all methods and only hands /panel to the
  panel when `panel` is enabled; with panel=false, /panel is a normal page path and non-GET requests get 405.
- Auth: password_hash in users.json, session cookie (HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax), session id regenerated on login, a
  CSRF token per session required as X-CSRF-Token header for changes. No sign up/installer: users are created with
  bin/blueprint (avoids an unauthenticated "create first admin" endpoint). Failed logins are delayed slightly.
- Saving: only blueprint fields that store a value are taken from the request, merged with the existing data and
  validated by the blueprint (422 with errors per field path); other data in the file stays. Empty values remove the
  key. Folder pages write page.md if it exists, otherwise page.json; page.content.md keeps the `content`.
  {slug}.php pages are read-only.
- Status = folder name: draft ".slug", unlisted "slug", listed "NN_slug" (appended after the last listed sibling,
  two digits like the existing content). New pages are always drafts. changeNum renumbers listed siblings.
- Frontend: Vue 3 + vue-router + Vite in panel/, built into public/panel/ (gitignored, `composer panel:build`).
  Native inputs (date/datetime-local/time/number/color/select/radio/checkbox/select multiple/textarea), native
  <dialog> for dialogs (no window.confirm). Structure rows as fieldsets with up/down/remove, tags as comma
  separated text with a datalist. Files, blocks and layout have no editor yet. Dark mode via prefers-color-scheme.
- structuredClone fails on Vue proxies -> JSON clone helper (all values are JSON anyway).
